# solidity-f: f folds Solidity (#1348). On an if's first line f folds it to its closing brace and
# f there unfolds it; on a line inside a function f folds the function. The file is written here,
# not in the project, which every other scenario counts the files of.
merl
wait Open a file (fuzzy)
run mkdir -p sol && printf 'pragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n\ncontract Vault {\n    uint256 total;\n\n    function deposit(uint256 n) external {\n        if (n == 0) {\n            revert();\n        }\n        total += n;\n    }\n}\n' > sol/Vault.sol
key q
wait merl exited: 0
merl sol/Vault.sol
wait A Vault.sol
key :
type 7
key Enter f
wait 1 line ⋯ }
key f :
type 10
key Enter f
wait 4 lines ⋯ }
key q
wait merl exited: 0
